  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Report door (#1696, PR #1798) puts the Debug info report into the GitHub new-issue URL. The \"Project:\" line of that report had the full path of the project file. That path usually has the user name in it, and the browser sends it to github.com.\n\n- `debug_info::shared_report` is a new form of the same report. It gives the project file and the machine file by file name only.\n- Review fix: `shared_report` passes its whole text through `report_scrub::scrub_paths`. Each path-like word in each field (status, GPU, machine vendor and model, machine file, project) changes to its last component. A status such as `open failed: <path>` thus sends only the file name.\n- A word starts a path when it starts with `/`, `\\`, UNC `\\`, a drive (`C:\\` or `C:/`), `~`, `./` or `../`, or when it has a `\\` or two or more `/`.\n- Delta-review fix (head `fa6d90ac5`): a path continues over spaces and marks to the last later word of the same line that has a separator. Thus `C:\\Users\\jane doe\\x.camproj`, `OneDrive - Contoso, Ltd\\Parts\\x.camproj` and `ACME (old) parts/x.camproj` all give `x.camproj`. A reason after a path (`<path>: access denied`) has no separator and stays. Two paths on one line merge into the last file name. One `/` alone (`mm/min`) is not a path.\n- Review fix: `report_scrub::last_component` (used by `file_name_only`) reads `/` and `\\` on every system. A Windows path in a project that opens on Linux or macOS thus gives its file name. A trailing separator gives the last folder name. A root, a drive, `.` or `..` gives `(no file name)`. A non-UTF-8 name reads lossily.\n- `report::report_body` uses `shared_report`. The Report door URL thus has no directory part of a path.\n- `debug_info::report` (the Debug info panel in the application) keeps the full paths. The status strip keeps its text. Both stay on the machine.\n- An unsaved project still reads `Project: unsaved`.\n- The report has no log excerpt, no tool library path and no recent-file list. Thus no other field needs a scrub. The title that the user types is the user's own text and is not scrubbed.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/2744-report-door-file-name.md` (updated: the rule and its known limits).\n\nThe look of the dialog does not change: only the data of the URL changes. No label, layout or window changes. No structural assertion changes. No snapshot PNG changes. Screenshots are not necessary.\n\n## Readings\n\nOn the merged tree (head `fa6d90ac5`, `origin/main` merged in):\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib --locked` (from `crates/ui`): 1290 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `report_tests::the_report_door_scrubs_a_status_path_that_is_not_the_project` (new). No saved project. The status is `open failed: C:\\Users\\someone\\Documents\\secret\\part.camproj: ...` and its POSIX twin `/home/someone/secret/part.camproj`. The body and the URL have `part.camproj`. They do not have `someone`, `secret`, `Documents`, `Users` or `home`, as typed or percent-encoded. The in-app report keeps the full path.\n- `report_scrub::tests::last_component_reads_both_separators_on_every_system` (new). Windows, POSIX, UNC and mixed forms, trailing separators and the no-file-name cases. The same asserts run on each system.\n- `report_scrub::tests::scrub_paths_keeps_only_the_file_name_of_each_path` (new). Drive, POSIX, `~`, UNC, quoted paths, folder names with spaces, a path before a reason, `mm/min` that stays, and a two-line text. Delta review: folder names with `,` (`OneDrive - Contoso, Ltd`), `)` (`ACME (old) parts`), `;` (`Shop; north`) and a closing quote (`\"Shop\" files`).\n- `report_tests::the_report_door_url_has_the_project_file_name_and_no_directory`. A project path in a user home directory and a status with that path. The body and the URL have `Project: bracket.camproj` and no directory part.\n- `report_tests::the_body_carries_the_questions_and_the_debug_report` (changed). It embeds `shared_report` and asserts `Project: unsaved`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The real browser and GitHub. The tests check the URL that the door builds, not the page that GitHub opens.\n- The tests ran on Windows only. The new asserts do not depend on the system, so they give the same result on Linux and macOS.\n- Known limits of the scrub (also in the decision file):\n  - A path to a folder keeps the last folder name.\n  - A relative path without a root keeps its first word when that word has no separator (`jane doe/x/y` keeps `jane`). No status message of the application has this form.\n  - A non-path text with two `/` (for example a GPU driver text) shrinks to its last part.\n\nChangelog: The Report door now sends only the file names of the project, the machine file and each path in the status line to GitHub, not the full paths on your disk.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2744\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
